Q1: If minting costs $15, do people unknowingly pay $22?
A: No. They receive a refund! The process is:
The user sends ~0.0072 ETH (~$22)
The contract swaps it for ~$22 USDC
The contract spends $15 USDC on minting
The contract returns ~$7 USDC to the user

I already implemented this in the contract (lines 265-269):
// Refund excess USDC if any
if (usdcReceived &gt; MINT\_PRICE) {
uint256 excess = usdcReceived - MINT\_PRICE;
require(usdc.transfer(msg.sender, excess), "Excess refund failed");
}

